ameter definition: user_id has default value None but is documented and validated as required. This misleads callers into thinking it's optional.", 'suggestion': 'Remove default value: def execute(self, user_id: str, **kwargs): to make requirement explicit at call sites'}, {'severity': 'minor', 'category': 'security', 'line': 46, 'message': "PII exposure in logs: user_id is logged in plaintext ('Authorization failed for user %s', user_id). Depending on user_id format, this may violate GDPR/data protection policies.", 'suggestion': "Hash or mask PII in logs: logger.warning('Authorization failed for user %s', hash_pii(user_id)) or use generic message: 'Authorization failed for requested operation'"}, {'severity': 'minor', 'category': 'compliance', 'line': 54, 'message': 'No exception handling around audit logging. If audit_service.log_action() fails, the exception propagates and the business operation may appear to have failed even if it succeeded, creating data inconsistency.', 'suggestion': "Add try-except around audit logging or use guaranteed audit queue: try: audit_service.log_action(...); except AuditError as e: logger.critical('AUDIT FAILURE: %s', e); alert_security_team()"}]

